From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:03:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi, netapi32: CreateSortedAddressPairs,
 NetUserModalsGet levels 0/1/3, NetUseAdd/NetUseDel

CreateSortedAddressPairs now accepts native IPv6 destinations and a source list, picks a source address per destination (route-aware for IPv4, scope and longest prefix otherwise) and sorts the pairs by RFC 6724 rules. NetUserModalsGet answers the stand-alone defaults for levels 0, 1 and 3. NetUseAdd maps to WNetAddConnection2 and NetUseDel to WNetCancelConnection2 instead of reporting success.

